// Generated by scripts/build-help-guide.mjs from magic-agent-docs. Do not edit.
export const HELP_GUIDE = "# Web console\n\n## Get started\n\n### Welcome to Magic Agent\n\nMagic Agent is an AI front office for your business. You describe your company, list what you sell and add what your agents should know. Your agents then answer every customer message on WhatsApp, Instagram, Messenger, Telegram, RCS, your website chat and phone, day and night.\n\nWhen a conversation needs a person, the agent hands it to your team. Everything the agents collect, from a booking to an order or a callback request, is filed for you to follow up.\n\nNote: \nEvery screenshot in this manual comes from **Skyline Habitat**, a demo real estate developer with four projects, three specialist agents, a website chat and a few dozen sample conversations. Your own workspace looks the same, filled with your business.\n\n#### What you can do with Magic Agent\n\n**Build an AI team**\n\nA front desk that greets every customer and hands them to the specialist who can help: sales, support, bookings.\n\n**Teach it your business**\n\nCompany facts, a product catalogue and a knowledge base the agents answer from, and nothing else.\n\n**Answer on every channel**\n\nWhatsApp, Instagram, Messenger, Telegram, RCS, a website chat widget, an AI voice widget and a phone line.\n\n**Step in when it matters**\n\nOne inbox for every conversation. Take over any chat with a reply, then hand it back.\n\n**Never lose a lead**\n\nEvery conversation is filed at a lead stage, and the follow-up desk nudges the quiet ones.\n\n**Market on WhatsApp**\n\nCampaigns, festival greetings, birthday wishes and event reminders, sent as approved templates.\n\n#### How this manual is organised\n\n**Get started**\n\nLearn the key ideas, sign in, take a tour of the console and work through the six-step setup.\n\n**Build your AI team**\n\nFill in your company profile, knowledge base and catalogue. Then create agents, test them in the playground and connect your channels.\n\n**Work your conversations**\n\nReply from the inbox, handle escalations, and follow up leads, contacts and orders.\n\n**Grow**\n\nRun WhatsApp marketing, set up alerts and integrations, and manage your team and billing.\n\n#### On the go\n\nMost of what you do in the console also works from the Magic Agent phone app: reading and answering chats, moving leads, checking orders. See the mobile app guide.\n\n#### Where to find Magic Agent\n\n| What | Where |\n| --- | --- |\n| Web console | agent.magicwebs.ai |\n| Phone app | Magic Agent on the App Store and Google Play |\n| Help | **Support** in the console's profile menu, or **Help & support** in the app |\n\n#### Need help?\n\nCan't find what you're looking for? Raise a ticket from **Support** in the console's profile menu, or from **Help & support** in the app, and the Magic Agent team will reply there and by email. See Get help.\n\n### Key concepts\n\nRead this page once before you set anything up. Every screen in Magic Agent builds on these ideas.\n\n#### Workspace\n\nA **workspace** is your business inside Magic Agent. It holds your company profile, agents, catalogue, knowledge base, channels, conversations and team. Nothing is shared between workspaces. If you run two businesses, each gets its own workspace.\n\n#### The front desk and specialist agents\n\nEvery workspace has one **front desk**. It answers first on every channel, works out what the customer needs, and silently hands the conversation to the **specialist agent** best placed to help. The customer never sees the handover; the conversation simply continues.\n\nIn the Skyline Habitat demo:\n\n| Agent | Customer-facing name | Takes over when… |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Front desk | Skyline Assistant | Always answers first |\n| Residential sales | Priya | The customer wants an apartment, villa or plot |\n| Commercial leasing | Arjun | The customer wants an office or showroom |\n| Home loan desk | Meera | The customer asks about loans, EMIs or partner banks |\n\nThe front desk chooses a specialist **only** from each agent's \"Hand over to me when…\" line. An agent without that line, or one that is still a draft, gets no conversations. See Agents.\n\n##### The two background desks\n\nTwo more desks come with your workspace and never chat with customers live:\n\n- **Follow-up desk**: reads each conversation about an hour after it goes quiet, files it at a lead stage, and sends at most a couple of polite nudges while the lead is still open.\n- **Marketing desk**: sends your campaigns, greetings, birthday wishes and event reminders on WhatsApp.\n\n#### What agents may say\n\nAgents answer only from what you give them:\n\n- **Company profile and facts**: who you are, hours, policies. Read by every agent on every reply.\n- **Catalogue**: the products and services you sell. Agents refuse to discuss anything not in the catalogue, and never quote a price that is not stored on the product.\n- **Knowledge base**: FAQs, policies, pages and documents the agents search when they need an answer.\n\nWhen an agent cannot answer, it says so, tells the customer the team will follow up, and logs a knowledge gap for you to fill.\n\n#### Record books\n\nA **record book** is something your agents collect and file, such as an order, a site visit, an appointment or a callback request. You decide what details to collect and what stages a record moves through. Agents then fill these in during conversations.\n\nEvery workspace has an **Orders** book for things sold from the catalogue. Add your own books for everything else. See Record books.\n\n#### Leads\n\nEvery conversation is also a **lead**. The follow-up desk files each one at a stage in your pipeline, such as *New enquiry*, *Qualified*, *Site visit booked*, *Won* or *Lost*. It matches the conversation against each stage's description, so the descriptions you write are what drive the pipeline. See Leads.\n\n#### Channels\n\nA **channel** is a way customers reach you: a WhatsApp number, an Instagram account, a Facebook Page on Messenger, a Telegram bot, an RCS sender, a website chat widget, an AI voice widget or a phone line. Each channel points to an agent, normally the front desk. See Channels.\n\n#### Human takeover\n\nYou and your team can reply in any conversation at any time. Your reply **takes over** the chat: the agent pauses (one hour by default) and then takes the chat back on its own, unless you hand it back sooner. When an agent escalates a conversation, it lands in Escalations.\n\n#### The 24-hour WhatsApp window\n\nWhatsApp only delivers free-form replies within 24 hours of the customer's last message. Outside that window, only **approved templates** go through. This is why marketing messages, alerts and late follow-ups always use templates. See Templates.\n\n### Sign in\n\nOpen agent.magicwebs.ai/login in your browser.\n\n**Enter your username**\n\nIn **Email or username**, type the email address you signed up with, or the **workspace ID** you were given (for example `skyline-habitat-demo`). Team members sign in with their own email.\n\n**Enter your password and press Sign in**\n\nIf this is the first time you are using an issued password, change it once you are in: open the profile menu at the bottom of the sidebar, then **Workspace settings → Access → Change your password**. New passwords need at least 12 characters.\n\n**Enter your two-factor code, if asked**\n\nIf two-factor authentication is on, type the six-digit code your authenticator app shows for Magic Agent. Lost your phone? Choose **Use a recovery code**. Each recovery code works once.\n\n#### One device at a time\n\nA login can be open in one place at a time. If you sign in while the same login is open elsewhere, Magic Agent shows **Already signed in elsewhere**, with the other device and when it was last active.\n\n- Choose **Sign out the other device and continue** to move the session to this device.\n- Choose **Cancel** to leave the other device signed in.\n\nIf the other device isn't yours, change your password as soon as you are in.\n\nTip: \nGive every person on your team their own login from the Team page instead of sharing the workspace password. Their replies are then signed with their own name, and nobody signs anyone else out.\n\n#### Forgotten password\n\nPasswords are stored hashed and cannot be recovered. Ask your administrator, or Magic Agent support, to issue a new one. A team member's password can be reset by the workspace owner from the **Team** page.\n\n#### Turn on two-factor authentication\n\nGo to **Workspace settings → Access → Two-factor authentication**:\n\n1. Choose **Set up an authenticator app** and scan the QR code with Google Authenticator, Microsoft Authenticator, 1Password or Authy (or type the key).\n2. Enter the six-digit code and press **Turn on**.\n3. **Save your recovery codes.** Copy or download them, then confirm **I have saved them**. They are shown only once.\n\nWhen two or fewer recovery codes are left, turn two-factor off and on again to get a fresh set.\n\n#### Sign out\n\nOpen the profile menu at the bottom of the sidebar and choose **Log out**.\n\n### \n\n---\ntitle: \"Tour of the console\"\ndescription: \"Find your way around the Magic Agent web console: the sidebar, the dashboard, the profile menu and the banners that can appear.\"\nkeywords: [\"navigation\", \"sidebar\", \"dashboard\", \"menu\", \"tour\"]\nicon: \"compass\"\n---\n\nThe console has a sidebar on the left and the page you are working on to the right. Collapse the sidebar with the panel icon at the top of the page.\n\n#### The sidebar\n\n| Item | What it is for |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Dashboard** | Messages, conversations, channels, setup progress and your agents at a glance |\n| **Genie** | An assistant that sets up and runs the workspace when you ask in plain words. See Genie |\n| **Team** | Your AI agents and the people who answer alongside them. See Team |\n| **Build** | Everything the agents work from: Company profile, Knowledge base, Catalogue, Record books, Agents, Custom tools and Channels |\n| **Inbox** | Every conversation on every channel. See Conversations |\n| **Escalations** | Conversations an agent handed to a person. The red number is how many are waiting |\n| **Leads** | Stages (the pipeline), Contacts, one entry per record book (for example *Site Visits* or *Orders*) and Payments |\n| **Marketing** | Overview, Audience, Campaigns, Events, Calendar and Templates |\n| **Social** | Comment rules, moderation, DM tools and activity for Instagram and Facebook. Appears once an Instagram account or a Facebook Page is connected |\n| **Notifications** | Alerts sent by WhatsApp or email when something happens. See Alerts |\n| **Integrations** | Google Sheets, Calendar and Drive, Razorpay, Magic Forms and Magic Reward |\n\nA section opens on its own when you are on one of its pages. A closed section shows a **red dot** when something inside it needs your attention. For example, **Build** shows one when the knowledge base has open knowledge gaps.\n\n#### The profile menu\n\nAt the bottom of the sidebar, click your workspace name to open:\n\n- **Workspace settings**: password, two-factor, message limits, webhook, AI assistant connector, theme. See Settings.\n- **Billing**: plan, wallet and message usage. See Billing.\n- **Support**: tickets with the Magic Agent team. See Support.\n- **Theme**: Light, Dark or System.\n- **Log out**.\n\n#### The dashboard\n\n- **Period**: switch between the last 7, 14 or 30 days in the top right.\n- **Messages** and **Conversations**: totals for the period, compared with the period before.\n- **Messages per day**: switch between **Chart** and **Values**.\n- **Conversations by channel**: a bar for each day, stacked by where conversations arrived from (WhatsApp, Instagram, Messenger, RCS, Telegram and web chat), with the day's escalated conversations in red below the line. Hover over a bar to see that day's total and its largest channels; the list underneath gives each channel's total for the period.\n- **Setup**: your progress through the six setup steps. Click any step to open it.\n- **Agents**: each agent with two buttons: test it in the playground, or configure it.\n\n#### Banners you may see\n\n| Banner | What it means |\n| --- | --- |\n| \"Your free trial ends …\" | Choose a plan before the date in Billing |\n| \"… The dashboard locks on (date) unless it is paid.\" | A payment failed. Choose **Fix payment** |\n| \"Wallet balance is low\" | Template messages stop once the wallet runs out. **Top up** the wallet |\n| Dashboard locked | Your agents **keep answering customers**. The console opens again as soon as a plan is active |\n\n### Genie\n\nGenie is the assistant built into Magic Agent. Tell it what you want in your own words and it does the work in your workspace: it looks things up, proposes the changes and makes them once you approve.\n\nOpen it from **Genie** in the sidebar, just under **Dashboard**.\n\n#### What you can ask\n\n| Area | For example |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Agents** | \"Create a sales agent that books site visits\", \"Rewrite Priya's prompt to be more formal\", \"Explain how my agents hand over to each other\" |\n| **Knowledge** | \"Add our refund policy\", \"What are customers asking that we can't answer?\", \"That answer about parking was wrong, it's free after 6pm\" |\n| **Catalogue** | \"Add a 2BHK at ₹85 lakh\", attach a photo of a price list and say \"Add these products\" |\n| **Records and leads** | \"Create a record book for appointments\", \"Move Pooja Joshi to Negotiation\", \"Show unpaid orders this week\" |\n| **Inbox** | \"Summarise today's conversations\", \"Assign the escalated chat to Arjun\" |\n| **Alerts** | \"WhatsApp me when a site visit is booked\", \"Why didn't yesterday's alert send?\" |\n| **Marketing** | \"Draft a Diwali greeting\", \"Remind contacts about the open house on Saturday\" |\n| **Reports** | \"How did this week go?\", \"How much did the agents cost this month?\" |\n\nClick a suggestion such as **Set up my business** or **How did this week go?** to start. Click the round arrows button next to them to see other suggestions.\n\n#### Approving changes\n\nGenie reads your workspace freely, but it asks before it changes anything. Each change appears as a card marked **Needs your approval** that shows exactly what will be saved.\n\n- Click **Approve** to make the change, or **Decline** to skip it. Genie won't try a declined change again; tell it what you'd like instead.\n- When Genie proposes several changes at once, use **Approve all** or **Decline all** above the message box.\n- Typing a new message while a card is waiting declines that card.\n\nClick **Approval required** under the message box to switch it to **Auto-apply**, and Genie makes changes straight away in that chat. Deleting anything still asks first. Click it again to go back.\n\nAbove each reply, a short line sums up what Genie did, for example *Looked at 2 things · made 1 change*. Click it to see each step, and click a step for its details. A step that didn't happen is marked **declined** or **failed**.\n\n#### Attach files\n\nClick the paperclip to attach up to five files: images, PDFs, Word, Excel, CSV or text. Genie can read a photo of a price list or menu and add the products, or add a brochure or policy document to the knowledge base.\n\n#### Chats\n\nYour conversations with Genie are listed under **Chats** on the left, grouped into **Today**, **Yesterday**, **Previous 7 days** and so on. Your chats are private to your login.\n\n- Click **+** to start a new chat.\n- Use **Search chats** to find an older one by its name.\n- Hover over a chat and click **⋯** to **Pin** it to the top, **Rename** it, **Copy link** to it or **Delete** it. You can also double-click a chat's name to rename it.\n- A chat with an amber dot has a change waiting for your approval.\n- Click the panel icon to hide the list and give the conversation the full width. Click it again at the top of the chat to bring the list back.\n\nIf Genie is taking too long, click **Stop**. Changes it has already made stay made.\n\n#### What Genie costs\n\nEach request you give Genie is a **Genie wish**. A wish costs the same as one marketing message to your home country, and is paid from your wallet. It appears as **Genie wish** under **Message usage** on the Billing page.\n\n- A request that fails is refunded.\n- Approving or declining a change is part of the same wish, not a new one.\n- When the wallet holds less than one wish costs, Genie asks you to top up before it starts.\n\nNote: \nGenie's AI usage is also listed as **Genie** in your usage breakdown.\n\n### Set up your workspace\n\nThe setup checklist walks you through everything your agents need to start answering well. Open it from **Setup** on the dashboard, or go to `/onboarding` in your workspace.\n\nThe dial shows your overall progress. Each card shows one step, how complete it is, and the next thing missing. Nothing here blocks the rest of the console: you can reopen and change any step at any time, and agents read the new version on their very next reply.\n\n#### The six steps\n\n**Company profile**\n\n**Needed:** company name, what the company does (two or three sentences; this is the most-read line in the whole setup), industry, a phone number or email, and currency, timezone and locale.\n\n**Optional:** tagline, website, address, and what the agents should call you.\n\n**Company facts**\n\nShort, specific lines every agent may state, such as opening hours, delivery areas, payment terms or booking amounts. One-tap topics are offered: Opening hours, Delivery, Payment terms, Lead time, Returns policy, Service area, Minimum order, Warranty.\n\nWarning: Saving replaces the whole list. A fact you remove is gone for every agent.\n\n**Agents**\n\nCreate at least one agent and take it live. Your first agent brings the front desk and the follow-up desk with it; there is nothing to set up for either. Every agent needs a **\"Hand over to me when…\"** line, or the front desk will never send it a conversation.\n\n**Knowledge base**\n\nAdd at least one source and wait until it shows **searchable**. Three or more sources is better. See Knowledge base.\n\n**Catalogue**\n\nAdd at least one product or service, each with a description. Store a price wherever you want agents to quote one. See Catalogue.\n\n**Enquiry stages**\n\nBuild the lead pipeline the follow-up desk files conversations into. Start with **Use the standard pipeline** (New enquiry, Qualified, Details collected, Quoted, Negotiating, Won, Lost) and adjust it. You need a **won** and a **lost** stage; otherwise customers who have already bought keep being chased.\n\n#### How the percentage works\n\nEach step's percentage is the share of its checks that are met; the overall dial is the average of the six steps. A step shows **Ready** once all its required checks are met. Optional checks only move the percentage.\n\nTip: \nAfter setup, open the playground and chat with your front desk the way a customer would. It's the quickest way to find gaps before customers do.\n\n## Build your AI team\n\n### Company profile\n\nEverything on this page goes into every agent's instructions on every reply. Filling it in well is the quickest way to make all of your agents more accurate at once.\n\nOpen it from **Build → Company profile**.\n\n#### Logo\n\nYour logo appears in the sidebar and at the top of the chat on your website. Choose **Upload logo** (PNG, SVG, JPG or WebP, up to 2 MB), or paste a link to one you already host and press **Use link**. The logo saves as soon as you pick it, and the page previews how it looks in both places.\n\n#### The business\n\n| Field | What agents use it for |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Name** | How agents introduce the company |\n| **Tagline** | A one-line summary shown under your name |\n| **Industry** | Sets the vocabulary agents reach for |\n| **What the business does** | The single most important field. Write two or three sentences in the words you want agents to use |\n| **Website**, **Support email**, **Support phone**, **Address** | Handed to customers when an agent cannot help directly |\n| **Locale** | Spelling and date formats, for example en-IN or en-GB |\n| **Timezone** | What counts as \"today\" for an agent, and when greetings go out |\n| **Currency** | What prices are quoted in |\n\n#### Company facts\n\nShort, checkable facts every agent may state: opening hours, site-visit times, booking amounts, delivery areas, partner banks. Add one row per fact, with a topic and what the agents should say.\n\nTip: \nWrite facts the way you would answer the question on the phone: \"Free site visits every day 10:00–18:00, with pick-up from anywhere in Ahmedabad on request.\" Short and specific beats complete and vague.\n\nPress **Save** at the top of the page when you are done.\n\n#### Welcome menu\n\nWhen someone opens with \"hi\" or something vague, the front desk can reply with a short message and one button for each thing you help with. Tapping a button hands the customer straight to the right agent.\n\n- **Message**: the text above the buttons.\n- **Heading** and **Footer**: optional; the heading can be text or a picture.\n- **Buttons**: up to 10, with titles of up to 20 characters. WhatsApp shows up to three as buttons; four or more become a list behind one button (**List button**, \"See options\" by default).\n- If every button has a picture, the menu goes out as a swipeable row of cards.\n\nBy default the menu has one button per live agent and updates itself as agents change. Editing a button switches the menu to custom; choose **Follow my agents** to go back.\n\nIn the demo, the menu offers **Buy a home**, **Office or showroom** and **Home loan help**.\n\n### Knowledge base\n\nThe knowledge base is where agents look up answers they don't already know from your company profile. Every source is split into short passages and indexed, so an agent can find the right passage in the middle of a conversation.\n\nOpen it from **Build → Knowledge base**.\n\nThe page has three tabs:\n\n- **Sources**: everything you have added.\n- **Wrong answers**: replies your team marked as wrong.\n- **Knowledge gaps**: questions agents could not answer.\n\n#### Add a source\n\n**Choose Add source**\n\nGive the source a **Title**. The agent sees it beside every passage, so make it descriptive, for example \"Booking and documentation process\".\n\n**Choose who can use it**\n\n**Available to**: every agent in the workspace, or only one agent.\n\n**Add the content**\n\nPick a tab:\n\n- **Paste text**: any prose an agent should be able to quote.\n- **FAQ**: question and answer pairs, separated by a blank line. Retrieval works noticeably better with Q and A.\n- **URL**: a page from your website. It is fetched once; choose **Reprocess** after the page changes.\n- **File**: PDF, plain text, Markdown, CSV, JSON or HTML. Scanned, image-only PDFs have no text to read; paste their content instead.\n\n**Wait for it to be searchable**\n\nThe source moves from *queued* to *indexing* to *searchable*, usually within seconds. If it shows *failed*, open it and choose **Reprocess**.\n\nYou can also add a file through the AI assistant connector: attach the PDF to the chat, or give the assistant a link to it, and ask it to add it to the knowledge base. The same file types work, up to 25 MB, and the source appears here like any other.\n\nTip: \nKeep one topic per source, for example \"Buyer FAQs\", \"Project amenities and locations\" and \"Booking and documentation process\". Small, focused sources give sharper answers than one huge document.\n\n#### Manage sources\n\nEach card shows its status, kind, how many passages it was split into, and which agents can use it.\n\n- **View & edit**: read the passages agents retrieve. Text sources can be edited, which re-indexes them. For URL and file sources, only the title and availability can change.\n- **Reprocess**: index the source again.\n- **Delete**: remove it. Agents stop using it immediately.\n\n#### Knowledge gaps\n\nWhen an agent is asked something it cannot answer, it tells the customer the team will follow up and logs the question here. Similar questions are grouped, most-asked first.\n\nFor each gap:\n\n- **Add answer**: write the answer. It is saved as an FAQ, so every agent answers it from now on.\n- **Dismiss**: ignore it.\n\nFilter between **Open**, **Answered** and **Dismissed**.\n\n#### Wrong answers\n\nWhen someone on your team marks an agent's reply as wrong in the inbox, it appears here with the sources the answer came from.\n\n1. Choose **Fix** and write the **Correct reply**. Agents use your correction ahead of anything that disagrees with it.\n2. Optionally edit the source the wrong answer came from.\n3. Choose **Send the right answer to the customer**. This works within 24 hours of the customer's last WhatsApp message.\n\nChoose **Not wrong after all** to unmark a reply.\n\n### Catalogue\n\nThe catalogue is the list of everything your agents may sell, quote or send. **Agents refuse to discuss anything that is not here, and never quote a price that is not stored on an entry.**\n\nOpen it from **Build → Catalogue**.\n\nTabs split entries into **Products**, **Services**, **Brochures** and **Other**. Search by name, or filter by category.\n\n#### Kinds of entry\n\n| Kind | Use it for | What agents do |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Product** | Something you make, stock or sell, such as a 3 BHK apartment | Describe it, quote its price, collect the questions before an order |\n| **Service** | Something you do, such as an interior fit-out or home-loan help | Same as a product |\n| **Brochure** | A document with a file, such as a project brochure | Send the file when a customer asks |\n| **Other** | Any other document, such as a price list | Send the file when a customer asks |\n\n#### Add an entry\n\nChoose **Add product** (the button follows the tab you are on). If you'd rather start from a worked example, the Catalogue step of the setup checklist offers sample entries. Picking one fills the form; nothing is saved until you press save.\n\n| Field | Notes |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Name** and **Description** | The description is what an agent answers \"what is it?\" with |\n| **Category** | Groups entries. Left empty, it goes under General or Services |\n| **Price** and **Unit** | Leave the price empty if your team quotes by hand; the agent is then told never to quote. The unit is said straight after the price, for example \"per unit (all-inclusive)\" |\n| **SKU**, **Tags** | Optional, for your own reference and search |\n| **Pictures** | Up to 8, under 5 MB each. The first is the thumbnail |\n| **Files** | For brochures and price lists: up to 10 files, 25 MB each |\n| **Attributes** | Extra facts the agent may state, such as carpet area or possession date |\n| **Specification questions** | What the agent must ask before it can record an order, for example *Which tower?* or *Will you need a home loan?* Each can be text, a number, pick-one, yes/no or a date, and can be required |\n| **Internal notes** | Read by the agent, never quoted to a customer |\n\nNote: \nSpecification questions are what turn a chat into a complete enquiry. An agent cannot file an order until every required answer is collected.\n\n#### Import or draft many entries at once\n\nChoose **Import** to open **Populate the catalogue**:\n\n- **Draft with AI**: Magic Agent drafts a starter catalogue from your company description. Review each entry before you rely on it.\n- **Import CSV**: download the **Sample CSV**, fill it in and upload it. Problems are listed by line and column, and nothing is imported until the file is clean. Entries are matched by name, so importing again updates existing entries instead of duplicating them.\n\n#### Add entries through an AI assistant\n\nWith the AI assistant connector set up, you can ask Claude, ChatGPT or another assistant to build the catalogue for you, files and pictures included. Attach a brochure or photo to the chat, or give the assistant a link to one, and say which entry it belongs to:\n\n- *\"Add a brochure called Tower B Brochure with this PDF.\"*\n- *\"Attach this price list to the 3 BHK apartment.\"*\n- *\"Add these photos to the Air Fryer.\"*\n\nThe assistant uploads the file to your catalogue, the same as choosing it in the form, so agents can send it to customers.\n\n| | Accepted |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Files** | PDF, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, text, CSV and more, up to 25 MB each |\n| **Pictures** | PNG, JPG, WebP or GIF, up to 25 MB each. On a new entry, the first picture is the thumbnail |\n\nAdding files or pictures to an existing entry keeps the ones it already has, and new pictures go after them. To take a file off, ask the assistant to remove it by name. To remove or reorder pictures, edit the entry yourself.\n\n#### View, edit or remove an entry\n\nUse the eye icon to view an entry without changing it: its pictures, price, description, the details and questions agents use, and its files, with a preview of the first PDF. Use the pencil icon to edit, and the bin icon to delete. Agents stop discussing a removed entry immediately. Orders already taken keep their own copy of the details.\n\n### Record books\n\nA **record book** is a list of things your agents collect in conversations, such as orders, site visits, appointments, memberships or callback requests. You choose the details to collect and the stages each record moves through. The agents get a tool to file into it.\n\nOpen it from **Build → Record books**.\n\nEvery workspace already has an **Orders** book for things sold from the catalogue. The Skyline Habitat demo adds three of its own: **Site Visits**, **Unit Bookings** and **Callbacks**.\n\n#### Create a record book\n\n**Choose New record**\n\nStart from a ready-made type (**Memberships**, **Appointments**, **Site visits** or **Quotations**), which brings its own details and stages. Or write your own.\n\n**Name it**\n\nGive the **Name** in the singular (\"Site Visit\") and the **Plural** (\"Site Visits\").\n\n**Say when to file one**\n\n**When should an agent file one?** is read by the agents, so write it as an instruction: \"File one when a customer agrees to visit a project on a specific date and time.\"\n\n**Create it**\n\nThe book opens on its **What to collect** tab, where you add the details and stages.\n\n#### What to collect\n\n- **Details to collect**: each has a label (the question as the customer sees it), a type (text, number, pick-one, yes/no or date), whether it is required, and an example. **Every required detail must be answered before an agent can file the record.** The agent goes back and asks instead of guessing.\n- **Stages**: what a record moves through after filing, for example *Requested → Confirmed → Visited → No-show → Cancelled*. The first stage is where every new record starts.\n- **Reference prefix** and **Reference type**: references look like `SV-8NNZSH` (random code) or 1, 2, 3 (serial number).\n- **Agents can look these up**: customers can ask \"when is my visit?\".\n- **Agents can change these**: customers can reschedule or cancel through the agent. Turn it off to route changes through your team.\n\nWarning: \nA new book collects nothing until it is switched on for an agent. Open the agent, go to **Knowledge & tools → What this agent records**, and turn the book on. See Agent editor.\n\n#### Work with filed records\n\nEach book also appears under **Leads** in the sidebar. The **Filed** tab lists every record with its reference, who it is about, the first details and the stage.\n\n- **Search** by name, phone or reference, and filter by stage.\n- Open a record to see its details and notes, and choose **Move** to change its stage. Moving a record can trigger an alert.\n- **Open conversation** jumps to the chat it came from.\n- **Add**: file one by hand. It gets a reference and fires the same alerts as one an agent files.\n- **Import**: upload a CSV or Excel file and map its columns.\n- **Export CSV**: download the list.\n- **Send payment link**: when Razorpay is connected. See Orders and payments.\n\nThe **Collecting / Paused** switch at the top stops or restarts collection without deleting anything.\n\n#### Connect a book to other systems\n\n- **Receive from elsewhere**: the book gets its own URL. Another system, such as a website form, can POST records to it. Capture a sample, then map each value to a field.\n- **Send elsewhere**: add a destination URL that receives each record when it is filed, updated or changes stage. **Recent deliveries** lists every attempt; choose **Resend** on a row to send it again to the same place, for example after fixing an endpoint that failed. A row the workspace webhook skipped because none is set is resent to this book's destinations instead, so records filed before you added a destination can still reach it.\n\n### Agents\n\nAgents are the AI teammates that talk to your customers. Open them from **Build → Agents**.\n\n#### The page at a glance\n\n- **Front desk card** (*Your AI team*): the front desk answers first on every channel and hands to your agents. It shows how many agents and conversations you have and the resolution rate. **Test routing** opens the front desk in the playground; **Configure** opens its settings.\n- **Your agents**: one card per specialist with its role, tools and stats (conversations, resolution rate, average response). Each has **Test** and **Configure**. Sort by last updated, name or conversations.\n- **Follow-up desk**: shows leads today, open leads and conversion rate. See Leads.\n- **Cards / Map**: switch between the card view and the agent map.\n\n##### The agent map\n\nThe map shows each channel, the agent it goes to, and who each agent can hand over to. Click an agent to change its status, handover line, knowledge and tools in a side panel, then **Save changes**.\n\n#### Create an agent\n\nChoose **New agent**. There are three ways to start:\n\n**Template**\n\nPick a ready-made agent: **Sales assistant**, **Lead qualifier**, **Customer support**, **Orders & after-sales**, **Appointment booking** or **Careers assistant**. Each says what it suits and when the front desk hands over to it. Optionally set the name customers see.\n\n**Describe**\n\nAnswer **What should this agent do?** in plain words and choose **Draft the agent**. Magic Agent writes the agent using your company description, facts and catalogue.\n\n**Blank**\n\nFill in **Internal name**, **Name customers see**, **Role** and **Front desk hands over when…**, then **Create agent**.\n\nWarning: \nEvery new agent starts as a **draft**. Drafts get no conversations. Review it in the agent editor, try it in the playground, then set its status to **Active**.\n\n#### How routing works\n\n1. A customer writes on any channel. The **front desk** answers first.\n2. It reads each **active** agent's **\"Hand over to me when…\"** line and picks the one that fits.\n3. It hands the conversation over silently. The specialist replies in the same chat.\n4. Specialists can hand on to each other the same way. A conversation is never handed back to an agent that already had it for the same message.\n\nFor routing to work:\n\n- Every specialist needs a clear \"Hand over to me when…\" line, written as a **condition**, for example: *\"Hand over to me when the customer asks about home loans, EMIs, eligibility, partner banks or the subvention payment plan.\"*\n- The agent must be **Active** and **Available for routing**.\n\nTip: \nTest routing from the front desk's playground. Each reply shows which agents it passed through when **Tool trace** is on.\n\n#### Agent statuses\n\n| Status | What happens |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Active** | Receives handovers and answers |\n| **Draft** | Gets no traffic. You can still test it in the playground |\n| **Paused** | Refuses every turn. The front desk can't be paused |\n\n### Agent editor\n\nOpen an agent from **Build → Agents → Configure**. The header shows the agent's name (click it to switch agents), its status (**Active**, **Paused** or **Draft**), **Test in chat** and **Save**.\n\nNote: Changes take effect on the agent's next reply after you press **Save**.\n\n#### Identity\n\n| Field | What to write |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Gender** | Sets the agent's face and the voice of spoken replies |\n| **Internal name** | Your name for it, for example \"Residential sales\". Customers never see it |\n| **Name customers see** | A first name reads better than a job title, for example \"Priya\" |\n| **Role** | For example \"Residential Sales Consultant\" |\n| **Objective** | What a successful conversation achieves |\n| **Job description** | The work step by step: how it opens, what it collects, how it closes |\n| **Opening line** | The first message customers see |\n\nThe **Voice** card turns on a microphone and **Listen** button in the website chat, and picks the voice.\n\n#### Routing\n\n- **Hand over to this agent when…**: the one line the front desk reads when choosing an agent. Write a condition, not a job description.\n- **Available for routing**: turn it off to take the agent out of every roster. It still answers on any channel pointed straight at it.\n- **Who this agent can hand on to**: the other agents it may pass a conversation to.\n\nFor the front desk, this tab lists who it can hand over to. The front desk is never handed a conversation and always stays active.\n\n#### Tone\n\n- **Should sound** and **Should never sound**: traits such as *warm*, *clear*, *pushy*, *robotic*.\n- **Formality** (Casual, Neutral, Formal), **Emoji** (Never, Sparing, Expressive), **Reply length** (Short, Medium, Detailed).\n- **Languages**, and **Mirror the customer's language**, which also handles mixes such as Hinglish.\n- **Human voice**: short, unpolished replies that read as if a colleague typed them. Asked directly, the agent still says it is an AI.\n\n#### Rules\n\n- **Always**: hard instructions, for example \"Always offer a free site visit once the customer shows interest in a project.\"\n- **Never**: hard limits, for example \"Never promise a discount\" or \"Never guarantee loan approval.\"\n- **Escalation policy**: when to hand over to a person.\n- **Additional instructions**: appended to the agent's instructions word for word.\n\nUniversal safety rules are added for you.\n\n#### Knowledge & tools\n\n- **Knowledge retrieval**: whether the agent searches the knowledge base automatically, and how many passages it reads per lookup.\n- **Built-in tools**: switch each on or off.\n- *Search knowledge base*\n- *Search catalogue*\n- *Get product requirements*\n- *Save contact detail*\n- *Escalate to human*\n- *Rich messages*: buttons, lists, media and contact cards on WhatsApp and web\n- *Transfer to another agent*\n- **What this agent records**: one switch per record book. Turning one on gives the agent the tools to file, find and update that kind of record.\n- **Integration tools**: Razorpay payment links, Magic Forms, Magic Reward and Google tools. Each is off until you turn it on here.\n- **Custom tools available here**: the custom tools this agent can call.\n\n#### Compiled prompt\n\nThis is exactly what the agent receives, built from everything you saved: identity, company profile, facts, rules and tools. Use it to check what an agent knows. Save your changes to refresh it.\n\n### Test in the playground\n\nThe playground is a private chat with one of your agents. It runs on the same engine that serves WhatsApp and the website chat, so knowledge lookups, the catalogue, record books, tools and routing all behave as they will for customers.\n\nOpen it from **Test** on an agent card, **Test in chat** in the agent editor, or **Test routing** on the front desk card.\n\n#### Have a test conversation\n\n1. Type in **Type as a customer would** and press Enter (Shift+Enter adds a new line). Or tap a starter such as *What do you sell?* or *I'd like to speak to someone*.\n2. Keep going until the agent files something or hands over. In the demo, asking the front desk for \"a 3 BHK near SG Highway\" hands you to Priya, who offers a site visit and files it.\n3. Press **Reset** to start a fresh conversation.\n\n#### Controls\n\n| Control | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Speak replies** | Reads each reply out loud |\n| **Tool trace** | Shows the tools each reply called, such as `search_products` or `file_site_visit`, and which agents it passed through |\n| **Reset** | Clears the conversation |\n| **Configure** | Opens the agent editor |\n\nTip: \nTest from the **front desk** to check routing end to end. Test a **specialist** directly to fine-tune its replies.\n\n#### Good things to test\n\n- Questions your FAQs answer, and a few they don't. Unanswered questions should appear under knowledge gaps.\n- A price question for an entry with a price, and for one without. The agent should not quote the second.\n- A full booking or order, to check the agent asks every required question before filing.\n- An angry or urgent message, to check the agent escalates to a person.\n\nNote: \nPlayground conversations appear in the inbox as web conversations, and records filed during a test are real records. Delete or move test records when you are done. A paused agent cannot be tested; set it to Draft or Active first.\n\n### Custom tools\n\nCustom tools let an agent do something the built-in tools can't, such as checking stock in your own system, looking up an order status, or searching your catalogue in a specific way. Only **enabled** tools reach the agents.\n\nOpen them from **Build → Custom tools**.\n\n#### Create a tool from a task\n\nThe quickest way is to describe the job in plain words.\n\n1. Choose **Create from a task**.\n2. Describe **The task**, for example \"Check if a unit type is still available in a project\".\n3. Optionally add **API details**: an endpoint, a curl command or a link to the docs.\n4. Choose who it is **Available to**: every agent, or one.\n5. Choose **Design the tool**. Turn on **Enable immediately** to use it straight away; otherwise it is saved as a draft for you to review.\n\n#### Create a tool by hand\n\nChoose **Manual** and fill in:\n\n| Field | Notes |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Display name** | Shown in the console |\n| **Tool name** | A short `snake_case` name, fixed once created |\n| **Description the model reads** | What the tool does and when to use it. This is what decides whether the agent calls it |\n| **When to use it** | Extra guidance for the agent |\n| **Kind** | **HTTP request** to your own system, or **Workspace data query** over products, orders or contacts |\n| **Parameters** | What the agent must fill in: name, type, required, description, fixed choices |\n| **Status** | Draft (not given to the agent), Enabled or Disabled |\n\nFor an **HTTP request**, set the method and URL (use `{{parameter}}` placeholders), headers and request body. For a **data query**, choose the table, the search parameter and a row limit.\n\nTip: \nWrite the description as \"what this does and when to use it\". The demo's tool reads: \"Look up which homes and units are in the catalogue and their availability notes. Use when a customer asks whether a type of unit is still available.\"\n\nEach tool card shows its status, kind, the agents it is scoped to and how often it has been called. Use the switch to enable or disable it. Tools added by an integration say **Managed by …**.\n\n### Channels\n\nA channel is a way customers reach you. Each channel points at an agent, normally the front desk.\n\nOpen them from **Build → Channels**.\n\nFilter by channel type, switch between grid and cards, and sort by last updated, most messages or name. Each card shows the channel's status, which agent answers, its number or handle, and message and customer counts.\n\nNote: Create at least one agent before connecting a channel.\n\n#### Website chat widget\n\nThe quickest channel to set up: live as soon as you paste one line onto your website.\n\n**Choose Create Web Widget**\n\nGive it a **Widget name** and leave **Agent that answers** on the front desk unless one agent should take everything.\n\n**Choose how visitors give their details**\n\n**In the chat**: the agent asks for a name and number. **Sign-in page first**: a short form before the chat opens.\n\n**Style the button**\n\nPick the icon, colour, position (bottom left or right), size and animation (none, pulse, bounce, wiggle or breathe), the tooltip, a **Teaser bubble**, and whether it **opens by itself after** a number of seconds. The preview updates as you go.\n\n**Add it to your website**\n\nCopy the **Embed code** from the channel card and paste it before `</body>` on your site. Or share the **Direct link** or **QR code**. Later style changes reach your site within a few minutes; you don't need to paste anything again.\n\nThis is what visitors see:\n\n#### WhatsApp\n\nYou need a number on the WhatsApp Business Platform (Meta), or through a BSP.\n\n1. Choose **Connect WhatsApp**.\n2. Fill in **Channel name**, **Agent that answers** (or *No agent — your team replies from the inbox*), **Phone number ID**, **Display number**, **WABA ID**, **Business ID** and **Access token**. Change **API base URL** only if you send through a BSP proxy.\n3. Choose **Create channel**, then copy the channel's **Callback URL** into your Meta app under **WhatsApp → Configuration → Webhooks**.\n\nA new WhatsApp channel starts paused until the callback is configured. Once it is live, the card shows a QR code and wa.me link for your number.\n\n#### Instagram\n\n1. Choose **Connect Instagram**, name the channel and pick the agent.\n2. Choose **Continue with Instagram** and sign in. Only business and creator accounts can be connected.\n3. In the Instagram app, turn on **Settings → Messages and story replies → Connected tools → Allow access to messages**.\n\nReplies go out within 24 hours of the customer's last message. Access renews automatically. Once connected, a **Social** section appears in the sidebar for comment rules and moderation.\n\n#### Messenger\n\nAnswer the Messenger conversations of a Facebook Page.\n\n1. Choose **Connect Messenger**, pick the agent, and optionally name the channel. Left blank, it takes the Page's name.\n2. Choose **Continue with Facebook** and sign in. You need to be an admin of the Page.\n3. When Facebook asks which Pages to share, tick the Page you want. If you share more than one, Magic Agent asks you to **Choose a Facebook Page**. Each Page is its own channel, so connect Messenger again for the next one.\n\nThe card shows the Page and a QR code that opens a Messenger chat with it. Replies go out within 24 hours of the customer's last message. The Page's comments can be automated from the **Social** section in the sidebar, see Social automation. If messages stop arriving, choose **Reconnect Messenger** from the channel's menu and make sure the Page is ticked.\n\n#### Telegram\n\nCreate a bot with **@BotFather**, choose **Connect Telegram** and paste the **Bot token**. Magic Agent connects the bot for you, so there is nothing else to set up. Only private chats are answered; groups are ignored.\n\n#### RCS\n\nChoose **Connect RCS**, paste the token from your RCS provider with the **Sender number**, then set the channel's **Callback URL** as the inbound webhook with your provider.\n\n#### AI voice widget\n\nA glowing sphere on your website that visitors tap to talk out loud, with no chat window. Choose **Create AI Voice Widget**, pick the agent, animation, position, size, colours, voice, greeting and captions, then paste the embed code. Your site must use https for the microphone to work.\n\n#### Phone line\n\nConnect a Plivo number so callers talk to an agent. Choose **Connect Phone Line**, enter the number, agent, voice and greeting, then paste the **Answer URL** and **Hangup URL** into an XML application in Plivo (method POST) and assign it to the number.\n\n#### Manage a channel\n\n- **Accept inbound messages**: switch a channel off and on.\n- **Edit**: change the name, agent or appearance.\n- **Reconnect Instagram** / **Reconnect Messenger**: sign in again, for example after changing your password or removing access.\n- **Rotate embed code** / **Rotate callback URL**: issue a new one. The old one stops working until you replace it.\n- **Delete channel**: customers can no longer reach you there. Conversations already received are kept.\n\nIf a channel has delivery trouble, its card shows **Last delivery problem** with the reason.\n\n## Work your conversations\n\n### Inbox and conversations\n\nThe inbox holds every conversation on every channel: WhatsApp, Instagram, Messenger, Telegram, RCS, the website chat and the playground. Open it from **Inbox** in the sidebar.\n\n#### Find a conversation\n\n- **Channel chips** at the top of the page, beside **Import from CRM**: all channels, or one.\n- **Buckets**: All, Open, Unread, Resolved.\n- **Search contact or message…**\n- **Filters** (the button beside the search box): agent, channel, **Answered by** (anyone, any team member, a named team member, the agent), **Assigned to**, **Lead stage**, **Tag**, last message (today, 7 or 30 days), and whether to include bots. Picking a team member under **Answered by** shows every conversation that person has replied in.\n\nEach row shows the contact, a preview of the last message, the message count, who is answering now, and badges such as **escalated**. Who is answering is the agent's name with a robot icon, or, once someone on your team has taken the thread over, that person's name with a person icon.\n\n#### Read a conversation\n\nThe customer's messages are on the left; the agent's and your team's replies are on the right, each labelled with who wrote it: the agent's name, or the name of the team member who sent the reply. Buttons, lists and files the agent sent show as they did for the customer.\n\nThe header shows:\n\n- the contact and status, the channel and last activity;\n- the **24-hour reply window** countdown for WhatsApp;\n- **Assign**: give the conversation to a team member, or unassign it;\n- the thread menu: set the status (open, escalated, resolved), **Resume agent now**, **Mark as bot**, **Delete conversation** (permanent; orders are kept) and the **Tool trace** switch.\n\n#### Take over a conversation\n\nYou can reply in any conversation at any time:\n\n**Type your reply and send it**\n\nSending a reply **takes over** the thread and **assigns it to you**. The thread shows a note saying you took it. The agent pauses for the time shown beside the box: 15 or 30 minutes, or 1 (the default), 2, 4, 8 or 24 hours.\n\n**Keep the conversation going**\n\nEvery reply you send restarts the timer. The header shows **You have this thread** with the countdown.\n\n**Hand it back**\n\nWhen the timer runs out, the agent takes the conversation back on its own. To hand it back sooner, choose **Resume now**.\n\n**Replying as** shows whose name signs the reply. Signed in with your own account, or as a human agent with your own login, it is always you. Signed in with the workspace's shared password, you choose who from the team. Use the emoji picker, or insert a product from the catalogue.\n\n##### Send more than text on WhatsApp\n\nThe **+** menu sends a photo (up to 5 MB), video (up to 16 MB), document (up to 100 MB), audio, location, contact card, up to three reply buttons, a list menu, a link button, a request for the customer's location, or a **template message**.\n\nWarning: \nWhatsApp only delivers free-form messages within 24 hours of the customer's last message. When the window has closed, the box says **Reply window closed — send a template with +**. Pick an approved template from the **+** menu instead. See Templates.\n\n#### Mark a wrong answer\n\nHover over an agent's reply and choose **Mark as wrong**. It goes to **Knowledge base → Wrong answers**, where you write the correct answer once and every agent uses it from then on. See Knowledge base.\n\n#### Details and notes\n\nThe right-hand panel (**Details and notes**) shows:\n\n- **Pipeline**: the conversation's lead stage and tags, and any records filed from it, each with a stage you can change.\n- **Contact**: phone, email, company and anything the agents saved.\n- **Notes**: notes for your team. Customers never see them.\n- **Agent**: whether the agent is paused and when it answers again.\n- **This thread**: status, start and last activity, message count, which agent it arrived at, who holds it (the agent, or the team member answering while the agent is paused), who it is assigned to, handovers and follow-up nudges sent.\n\n#### Start a conversation\n\nChoose the **+** button beside the filters (**New conversation**), pick an existing contact and the agent that should hold the thread, then **Open thread**. Nothing is sent until you write a message.\n\n### Escalations\n\nAn agent **escalates** a conversation when it needs a person: an upset customer, a complaint, a request to speak to a manager, or anything its escalation policy says to pass on. Escalated conversations wait in **Escalations** until someone sets them back to open or resolves them.\n\nOpen them from **Escalations** in the sidebar. The red number shows how many are waiting.\n\n#### Handle an escalation\n\n1. Open the conversation and read what happened.\n2. Reply. Your reply takes over the thread and pauses the agent.\n3. When it's sorted, set the status to **Resolved**, or back to **Open** to let the agent carry on.\n\nTip: \nEscalations also reach you away from your desk: as push notifications in the mobile app, and as WhatsApp or email alerts if you set one up for the *Escalation* event.\n\n#### Handover rules\n\nHandover rules decide **who** gets an escalated conversation. Without rules, escalations stay unassigned until someone picks them up.\n\nOpen them from **Team → Handover rules**. The first rule that matches wins.\n\n| Setting | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| **When this agent escalates** | Any agent, or one specific agent |\n| **To the department** | Any, Sales, Support, Accounts or Other |\n| **Assign to** | One or more people. With several, they take turns. Anyone set to *Away* is skipped |\n| **Pause the agent** | The agent stops replying so the person can take over |\n| **Hand back to the agent after** | From 15 minutes to 24 hours |\n| **Rule is on** | Switch a rule off without deleting it |\n\nUse **Move up** and **Move down** to change the order.\n\n#### The escalations desk for team members\n\nTeam members can work from a focused view at `/desk`. It shows only escalations, with **All**, **Unread** and **Assigned to me**. Replies are signed with the member's own name, and **Resolve** hands the conversation back to the agent. **Open the dashboard** goes to the full console.\n\n### Leads pipeline\n\nEvery conversation becomes a lead. About an hour after a conversation goes quiet, the **follow-up desk** reads it, files it at the stage that fits, applies tags, and sends at most two polite nudges while the stage is still open.\n\nOpen the pipeline from **Leads → Stages**.\n\n#### Read the board\n\n- **Stage chips** across the top show how many leads are at each stage. **Not yet reviewed** holds conversations the desk hasn't read yet.\n- Switch between **Kanban**, **Cards** and **List** views.\n- Filter by search, channel, status, time and tag.\n\nEach lead card shows the contact, the last message, the desk's reason for the stage, a message count and who handled it. A pin icon means the lead was **filed by hand**, so the desk won't move it.\n\n#### Move a lead\n\n- Drag a card to another column in Kanban, or\n- change the stage from the stage selector on the card.\n\nFiling a lead by hand **pins** it: the follow-up desk's reviews leave it there. Choose **Unfile** to hand the decision back to the desk.\n\nFollow-up status on each card:\n\n| Status | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| Can still be nudged | The desk may send a follow-up |\n| Nudge limit used | Two nudges have gone out |\n| Stage is closed | Won or lost; no more follow-ups |\n| Not reviewed yet | The desk hasn't read it |\n\n#### Set up stages\n\nChoose **Manage stages**.\n\nEach stage has:\n\n- **Name**, for example *Site visit booked*.\n- **What belongs here**: the test the follow-up desk applies to a conversation. Describe the situation, not the label: *\"A site visit has been agreed for a specific date, or a Site Visit record has been filed in the conversation.\"*\n- **Outcome**: **Open** (still in play), **Won** or **Lost**. Won and lost stop the follow-ups.\n\nWarning: \nThe descriptions **are** your pipeline: the desk files conversations by matching them against these lines. Keep a won and a lost stage, or customers who have already bought keep being chased. Deleting a stage returns its leads to unfiled.\n\n#### Tags\n\nChoose **Manage tags** to create labels such as a type of enquiry, a priority or a source.\n\n- A tag **with a description** is applied by the follow-up desk on its own, for example *Hot lead: \"They want to buy within the next 30 days, have a budget ready, or ask about booking a specific unit.\"*\n- A tag **without** a description is only applied by hand.\n\nOnce someone changes a lead's tags by hand, the desk leaves them alone.\n\nNote: \nIf the page says **No follow-up desk yet**, choose **Create the follow-up desk**. Nothing is filed or followed up until the workspace has one.\n\n### Contacts\n\nOpen **Leads → Contacts** for a table of everyone who has talked to your agents.\n\n#### Columns\n\n| Column | What it shows |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Name**, **Phone / Email** | Who they are |\n| **Handled by** | The agent or person who holds the conversation |\n| **Lead stage** | Where the follow-up desk filed them, or *Not reviewed* |\n| One column per record book | The stage of their latest record, for example *Requested* under Site Visits or *Token pending* under Unit Bookings |\n| **Remark** | A note for your team |\n| **Last seen** | When they last wrote |\n\n#### Find people\n\nSearch by name, number, owner or remark, and filter by channel, status (including *Never messaged*) and last seen. Choose **Show more** to load more rows.\n\n#### Edit a contact\n\nClick a contact to edit their **Name**, **Phone**, **Email**, **Company** and **Remark**. The remark is for your team only and never shown to the customer. The follow-up desk also records there why it messaged someone.\n\nTip: \nTo import or export contacts, or add people who haven't written in yet, use Marketing → Audience.\n\n### Orders and payments\n\n#### Orders and other records\n\nEach record book has its own entry under **Leads** in the sidebar, for example **Orders**, **Site Visits**, **Unit Bookings** or **Callbacks**.\n\nFrom a book's **Filed** tab you can:\n\n- search by name, phone or reference, and filter by stage;\n- open a record to read every detail and **Move** it to the next stage;\n- **Open conversation** to see how it was collected;\n- **Add** a record by hand, **Import** a CSV or Excel file, or **Export CSV**.\n\nNote: \n**Orders** is the book for things sold from the catalogue. If the Orders page says the workspace \"does not have its Orders book yet\", use **Open Record books** and create it there.\n\n#### Payments with Razorpay\n\nOnce you connect Razorpay, agents and your team can send payment links, and **Payments** appears under Leads.\n\n##### Send a payment link\n\n1. Choose **New payment link**, or **Send payment link** on a record.\n2. Enter the **Amount (₹)**, or an **Order reference**. With a reference, you can leave the amount blank to charge the order's total.\n3. Fill in **What it is for** and the customer's name, phone and email.\n4. Choose **Create link**. It is copied to your clipboard. Razorpay can also text and email it to the customer.\n\nWhen the customer pays, the record moves to the stage you chose in the Razorpay settings.\n\n##### Track payments\n\nFilter by **All**, **Open**, **Paid**, **Part paid**, **Expired** or **Cancelled**. Each row shows who sent the link (an agent or *Team*), the amount and status. The row menu can copy or open the link, open the conversation, refresh the status or cancel the link.\n\nTo let an agent send links on its own, turn on the Razorpay tools for that agent under **Knowledge & tools** in the agent editor.\n\n## Marketing\n\n### Marketing overview\n\nThe **marketing desk** sends WhatsApp messages to your contacts on a schedule:\n\n- **Campaigns**: one-off broadcasts such as offers, launches and announcements. See Campaigns.\n- **Greetings**: festivals and special days. See Calendar.\n- **Birthday wishes**: sent to each contact on their birthday. See Audience.\n- **Event reminders**: before, on and after your own events, each written by the desk. See Events.\n\nEvery message lands in the contact's conversation, so the inbox shows it, and a reply carries on from it with your agents.\n\n#### Before anything can send\n\n**Connect a WhatsApp number**\n\nMarketing goes out from your workspace's WhatsApp number. Until one is connected, the marketing pages show **Connect WhatsApp first** and nothing scheduled will send. See Channels.\n\n**Get a template approved**\n\nEverything the desk sends is an **approved WhatsApp template**, because only templates reach people outside the 24-hour window. Write one and apply it to Meta. See Templates.\n\n**Have people to send to**\n\nEveryone who has written to you on WhatsApp is already in your audience. Import more contacts who agreed to hear from you. See Audience.\n\n**Keep your wallet topped up**\n\nTemplate messages are charged to your wallet. When the wallet can't cover them, they are held back. See Billing.\n\nChoose **Tone and rules** at the top of any marketing page to change how the marketing desk writes.\n\n#### Read the results\n\nPick a period (7, 30 or 90 days) to see:\n\n- **Your WhatsApp number**: quality rating, messaging limit and how much you sent in the last 24 hours. A red rating pauses smart campaigns; a yellow rating makes them wait 48 hours and halve the next wave.\n- **Messages sent**, **Delivered**, **Read**, **Replied**, **Link clicks**, **Orders and bookings**, **Unsubscribed** and **Spent on campaigns**.\n- **Messages sent each day**.\n- **Audience**: who can be messaged, new contacts, and unsubscribes. You're warned when unsubscribes go above 2%.\n- **What went out**: each campaign with sent, read, replied, clicked and orders.\n\nShortcuts at the top: **Import contacts**, **New event** and **New campaign**.\n\n### Audience\n\nThe audience is everyone your marketing can reach. Open it from **Marketing → Audience**.\n\n#### The page at a glance\n\n- **Tiles**: who **Can be messaged**, who is **Unsubscribed**, how many **Lists** you have, and how many **Complete contacts**.\n- **Rail** on the left: *Everyone* (all contacts, unsubscribed), your **Categories** (up to 10, sorted automatically by Agent Check), and your **Lists**.\n- **Table**: each contact with category, the fields you choose under **Columns**, tags and subscription status.\n\nSelect up to 500 people at a time to **Move to** a category, **Tag**, **Add to list**, **Save as list** or **Remove from list**.\n\n#### Add people\n\n- **Add by hand**: one person at a time, with name, category, email, company, birthday, tags, notes and the **Gets marketing messages** switch.\n- **Import contacts**: bring in a whole list (below).\n- Everyone who writes to you on WhatsApp is added automatically.\n\n#### Import a contact list\n\n**Upload**\n\nName the list and set the **Country code** for numbers written without one. Upload a CSV (Google Contacts, Excel and others work), or **Paste a list** with one person per line: name, phone number, note. Up to 10,000 people per import.\n\n**Map columns and clean up**\n\nMatch your columns to name, phone, email, company and birthday. Basic cleaning can skip rows with no phone number and remove repeated numbers.\n\n**Confirm consent**\n\nTick that these people agreed to hear from you on WhatsApp. Messaging people who did not agree gets your number reported and restricted.\n\n**Agent Check**\n\nMagic Agent checks every contact in batches and sorts them into **Ready**, **Needs a look**, **Problems**, **Repeats** and **Left out**. You can leave the page while it works.\n\n**Review and save**\n\nFix names or numbers, change categories, keep or put back rows, then save. Nobody is added until you review.\n\n#### Export\n\nUse the export menu to download all contacts, only those who can be messaged, the unsubscribed, or one category or list.\n\n#### Weekly message limit\n\nSet a maximum number of marketing messages per person per week, or **No limit**. It applies to campaigns and event reminders. Birthday wishes don't count.\n\n#### Birthday wishes\n\nEach contact whose birthday is today gets your birthday template once, at the hour you choose.\n\n1. Make a template with the **Birthday** occasion and apply it to Meta. See Templates.\n2. In the **Birthday wishes** card, pick the **Template** and the **Send at** time, and switch it on.\n\nIt won't send until the template is approved.\n\n#### Unsubscribes\n\nMarketing templates can carry a **Stop messages** button. Anyone who taps it is unsubscribed and gets no more marketing.\n\n### WhatsApp templates\n\nWhatsApp only delivers **approved templates** to people who haven't written to you in the last 24 hours. Every campaign, greeting, birthday wish and event reminder goes out as one.\n\nOpen them from **Marketing → Templates**.\n\nEach card previews the message as it will look on a phone, with a status badge:\n\n| Badge | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Not applied** | Saved here, not yet sent to Meta |\n| **In review** | Meta is reviewing it, usually within minutes, sometimes a day |\n| **Approved** | Ready to send |\n| **Changed** | Edited after approval; it won't send until the change is approved |\n| **Rejected** | Meta turned it down. Edit and apply again |\n| **Linked** | Linked to a template approved elsewhere |\n\n#### Create a template\n\nChoose **New template**.\n\n| Field | Notes |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Name** | For you |\n| **Occasion** | Festival, Birthday, Event reminder, Offer or General |\n| **Category** | Marketing, Utility or Authentication. This is what Meta approves it as, and what every send is billed at |\n| **Type** | Standard, or Carousel (up to 10 swipeable cards) |\n| **Header** | None, Text (up to 60 characters), Image or Video |\n| **Message** | The body. Use `{{name}}`, `{{business}}` and `{{event}}`, and for event reminders `{{date}}`, `{{venue}}` and `{{message}}`. **Write it for me** drafts one |\n| **Footer** | A small grey line, up to 60 characters, no variables |\n| **Buttons** | Up to 10: quick replies, at most 2 website links and 1 call button. Labels up to 25 characters |\n\nTip: \nAdd a **Stop messages** quick reply to marketing templates. Anyone who taps it is unsubscribed, which protects your number's quality rating.\n\nWarning: \nMeta rejects a message that starts or ends with a variable, or puts two variables side by side. Headers and footers can't hold variables.\n\n#### Get it approved\n\nChoose **Save and apply to Meta**. The status moves to **In review**, then **Approved**. Press **Check status now** to refresh, or **Sync templates** to pull in templates approved in WhatsApp Manager.\n\nEditing an approved template pauses it until Meta approves the change.\n\n#### Templates in the demo\n\n| Template | Occasion | Used for |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Festival greeting | Festival | Christmas, New Year and Makar Sankranti greetings |\n| Birthday wish | Birthday | Birthday wishes |\n| Event reminder | Event reminder | Open house and Home Loan Mela reminders, with the desk's line in `{{message}}` |\n| Year-end offer | Offer | A campaign with an image header and a *Book a site visit* button |\n\n### Campaigns\n\nCampaigns are one-off broadcasts: offers, launches, announcements and festival greetings. Open them from **Marketing → Campaigns**.\n\nThe list shows each campaign's status, how many it went to, and how many were sent, read, replied to or failed.\n\n#### Create a campaign\n\nChoose **New campaign**, then pick a mode.\n\n**Smart campaign (safest)**\n\nSends in daily waves, most engaged contacts first. Watches your number's quality and limits, and pauses itself if something goes wrong. Best for large audiences.\n\n**Manual campaign**\n\nYou choose when it goes and how fast. Best for small, warm audiences.\n\n##### Compose it\n\n**Name it**\n\nFor example \"Year-end Tower C offer\".\n\n**Choose who gets it**\n\n**Everyone subscribed**, or **Choose who** by category, list, tag or record book (and its stages). Narrow further with **Only people who…**:\n- read but didn't reply (last 30 days)\n- ordered in the last 30 days\n- ordered before, but not in 90 days\n- have been silent for 90 days\n- never read a marketing message\n\nUse **Leave out anyone on** to exclude a list.\n\n**Choose what they read**\n\nPick an approved template and fill in its blanks.\n\n**Set the details**\n\n- **Track link clicks** gives each person their own short link.\n- **Replies go to** the front desk or a specific agent.\n- **Schedule** for a day and time, or send now.\n- For manual campaigns, set the **Speed** and optionally **Send at each person's best time**.\n\n**Before it goes** shows how many will receive it, how many are left out (unsubscribed or over the weekly limit), the estimated cost and your wallet balance. If the wallet doesn't cover everyone, sending stops when it runs out.\n\n##### Launch it\n\n- **Manual**: choose **Send now** and confirm. This can't be undone.\n- **Smart**: choose **Review plan** to see the waves, days, people and cost per wave, then **Launch smart campaign** or **Save as draft**.\n\n##### Smart campaign safety checks\n\nA smart campaign:\n\n- checks your number's quality before every wave, and pauses on a red rating, spam reports or a paused template;\n- on a yellow rating, waits 48 hours and halves the next wave;\n- holds for a day when unsubscribes pass 1.5%, and pauses at 3%;\n- never uses more than 80% of your daily limit, and spreads each wave over about two hours.\n\n#### Follow a campaign\n\nOpen a campaign to see its total, sent, read, replied and clicked rates, orders and bookings, failures, unsubscribes and cost. It also shows a send-to-reply funnel, when people read it, and why some messages didn't arrive.\n\nActions:\n\n- **Pause** / **Resume**, **Stop sending**, or **Delete** if it hasn't started\n- **Send again** to people who didn't read it, or to those it failed for\n- **Duplicate**\n- Filter **Recipients** by outcome, export a CSV, or **Save as a list** to follow up\n\n### Events\n\nAn event, such as an open house, a launch or a workshop, gets a series of WhatsApp messages: an announcement, reminders, a message on the day and a follow-up afterwards. The **marketing desk writes each one** from your event details, and reads replies as RSVPs.\n\nOpen events from **Marketing → Events**.\n\n#### Before you start\n\nAll reminders go out with one approved template of the **Event reminder** occasion. The desk's line for each reminder fills its `{{message}}` blank. If you have none, choose **Create the reminder template** on the alert at the top. See Templates.\n\nWarning: \nUntil an event has a template that can send, its reminders are **drafts** and nothing goes out. The event card says so.\n\n#### Create an event\n\nChoose **New event** and fill in:\n\n| Field | Example from the demo |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Event** | Skyline Greens Open House |\n| **Day** and **Starts at** | 6 December, 11:00 |\n| **Where** | Skyline Greens sample villa, Shela |\n| **What it is** | Families walk through the 4 BHK villa, meet the architect, see the clubhouse and get on-the-spot loan eligibility checks |\n| **Offer** | Free modular kitchen upgrade on bookings made at the open house. It is only ever repeated as written |\n| **Link** | An optional page for details |\n| **Who's invited** | Everyone, or a chosen group |\n| **Messages** | Which reminders to send, from two weeks before to one week after |\n| **Template** | Your event reminder template |\n\nBy default you get reminders 3 days before, the day before, on the day and the day after. Each reminder can go to a different group: everyone invited, everyone but those who said no, those who said yes or maybe, those who came, or those who said yes but didn't come.\n\nChoose **Save and schedule**, or **Save as draft**.\n\n#### Review each reminder\n\nThe desk writes each reminder as soon as you save, and the event card shows them with their status. Open one to edit the message, **Rewrite** it, **Skip this one** or **Send now**.\n\nNote: If your template uses `{{venue}}`, fill in **Where**, or the reminder can't send.\n\n#### Guests and check-in\n\nChoose **Guests** on the event card to see who is going, who might come and who can't, and who came.\n\n- **Check in** a guest by number (and name, if new) and **Mark as came**.\n- Change anyone's RSVP by hand, or mark **Everyone going came**.\n\n### Calendar and greetings\n\nThe calendar shows everything the marketing desk will send, by day: festival greetings, one-off sends, event reminders and birthdays. Open it from **Marketing → Calendar**.\n\n- Move between months, or jump back to **Today**.\n- Click a day to see what goes out and to **Schedule on this day**.\n- **Festivals coming up** lists the next four months of festivals. Lunar festival dates can shift by a day between regions, so check before you schedule.\n\n#### Schedule a greeting\n\n**Choose Schedule greeting**\n\nOr pick a festival from **Festivals coming up**.\n\n**Fill it in**\n\n- **Title**: fills `{{event}}` in your template, for example \"Christmas\".\n- **Day** and **Send at**: in your workspace's timezone.\n- **Template**: an approved greeting template, or *None yet* to keep it as a draft.\n\n**Schedule it**\n\nChoose **Schedule**, or **Save draft**. You can also **Send now** or **Remove from calendar**.\n\nA greeting goes to every subscribed WhatsApp contact.\n\nWarning: \nA greeting with an unapproved template fails on the day. Make sure its template shows **Approved** in Templates beforehand.\n\nIn the demo, Christmas, New Year and Makar Sankranti greetings are scheduled as drafts, waiting for the Festival greeting template to be approved.\n\n### Social automation\n\nOnce you connect an Instagram account or a Facebook Page on Messenger, a **Social** section appears in the sidebar. Messages are answered by the account's agent like any other channel. This section adds automation for comments and stories.\n\nIf you have more than one account or Page, pick the one you are working on from the menu at the top. Facebook Pages are marked **(Facebook)**.\n\n#### Overview\n\nThe last seven days at a glance: comments, public replies, DMs sent, comments moderated and story mentions, with links to each tool and recent activity.\n\n#### Comment rules\n\nA comment rule answers a matching comment with a public reply, one private message, or both. A classic example is \"comment PRICE and we'll DM you\". On Instagram the private message is a DM. On Facebook it arrives in the commenter's Messenger.\n\nChoose **New rule**, or start from a preset: **Comment-to-DM** or **Thank every commenter**.\n\n| Setting | Options |\n| --- | --- |\n| **When** | **Comment has a keyword** (whole words, comma-separated), or **Any comment** |\n| **Where** | **On every post**, or **On chosen posts** (up to 20) |\n| **Public reply** | **Written here** (one per line, picked at random; `{{username}}` becomes the commenter's @handle on Instagram or first name on Facebook), **AI writes it** (never quotes prices), or **No reply** |\n| **Private DM** | The message, plus an optional button with a link. One message per comment, within 7 days |\n| **Once per person** | Answer each person only once |\n| **Live** | Switch the rule on or off |\n\nA comment fires only one rule: a keyword rule before a catch-all, and a rule for chosen posts before one for every post. Messages sent this way land in the inbox, and the agent picks up any reply.\n\nNote: \nA Facebook Page connected before comment automation was available shows **Reconnect to turn on comment automation**. Choose **Reconnect Facebook** and allow MagicAgent to manage the Page's posts and comments.\n\n#### Moderation\n\nModeration runs on every new comment **before** any rule.\n\n- **Moderate comments**: the main switch.\n- **What happens to a flagged comment**: **Hide** (still visible to the writer and their friends or followers) or **Delete** (gone for good).\n- **Block links**, and **Blocked words** (whole words).\n- **Screen with AI**: catches insults, hate, threats and spam, and leaves genuine complaints up. Billed as AI usage.\n\n#### DM tools\n\nInstagram only.\n\n- **Story mention reply**: an automatic thank-you when someone mentions you in their story. Use `{{username}}`.\n- **Ice breakers**: up to four questions shown to someone opening a DM with you for the first time.\n\n#### Activity\n\nEvery comment and story mention, and what was done about it. Kept for 90 days.\n\n## Automation\n\n### \n\n---\ntitle: \"Alerts\"\ndescription: \"Send a WhatsApp template or an email automatically when a record is filed or moves stage, an agent escalates, an agent hits a knowledge gap, or another system calls in.\"\nkeywords: [\"alerts\", \"notifications\", \"email\", \"whatsapp\", \"record filed\", \"escalation\", \"webhook\"]\nicon: \"bell\"\n---\n\nAlerts tell you, your team or the customer when something happens. Use them to email the sales team about every new site visit, to WhatsApp the customer when their booking is confirmed, or to message a manager when an agent escalates.\n\nOpen them from **Notifications** in the sidebar.\n\n#### Senders\n\nAt the top, two cards show where alerts go out from:\n\n- **WhatsApp**: your connected WhatsApp number. WhatsApp alerts can only send approved templates.\n- **Email**: ready out of the box. Under **Senders**, set the sender name and reply-to address, and **Send a test email**.\n\n#### Create an alert\n\nChoose **New alert**.\n\n**Name it**\n\nFor example \"Email sales on new site visit\".\n\n**Pick the event**\n\n| Event | Fires when |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Record filed** | An agent or your team files a record. Narrow it to one record book |\n| **Record updated** | A record's details change |\n| **Stage changed** | A record moves stage. Narrow it to one book and the stage it moved to |\n| **New order** | An order is filed in the Orders book |\n| **Escalation** | An agent hands a conversation to a person |\n| **Knowledge gap** | An agent can't answer a question from the knowledge base |\n| **Incoming webhook** | Another system POSTs to the alert's own URL |\n\n**Choose WhatsApp or email**\n\n- **WhatsApp**: pick a synced, approved template and fill each blank with text or a `{{variable}}` from the event.\n- **Email**: pick an email template (see below).\n\nThe dialog lists every variable the event offers, such as the customer's name or the record's reference and details. Click one to copy it.\n\n**Choose who gets it**\n\n**The customer**, team members, or numbers and email addresses you type.\n\n**Save and test**\n\nChoose **Create alert**, then **Send test** to send it once with made-up details.\n\n#### Email templates\n\nOn the **Email templates** tab, choose **New email** and write the **Subject** and **Message** in plain text or HTML. Use `{{variables}}` from the event, for example `{{record.reference}}`, `{{record.person.name}}` or `{{record.details.visit_date}}`. Preview it, then **Save email**.\n\n#### WhatsApp templates\n\nThe **WhatsApp templates** tab lists templates synced from WhatsApp Manager. Approve them there first, then choose **Sync templates**. Pick one to **Send it now** or **Use in an alert**.\n\n#### Activity\n\nThe **Activity** tab lists every alert, test and message sent by hand, who it went to and when. Scroll down and older sends keep loading.\n\nNarrow the list with:\n\n- **Search** — a number, email address, template name, subject or words from the message.\n- **Alert** — one alert, **Any alert**, **Tests** or **Sent by hand**.\n- **Channel** — WhatsApp or Email.\n- **Status** — Sent, Failed or Skipped. The counts above the table show how many of each match your other filters; select one to show only those.\n- **Period** — Today, the last 7, 30 or 90 days, or All time.\n\nChoose **Clear** to reset the filters, or **Export CSV** to download the sends loaded so far.\n\nSelect a send to see the full message and, for anything that didn't go, **Why it did not send**. Each alert card also shows sent and not-sent counts and its last error — select the counts to open **Activity** filtered to that alert. Use the switch on a card to turn an alert off.\n\n### Integrations\n\nIntegrations give your agents new abilities. Open them from **Integrations** in the sidebar.\n\nFilter by **Magic Apps**, **Google**, **Payments** or **Other**. Each card shows whether it is connected. Open one to see what it can and can never do, what agents can do with it, an FAQ and how to connect it.\n\nWarning: \nConnecting an integration doesn't hand it to any agent. Every tool it adds is **off** until you switch it on for an agent under **Knowledge & tools** in the agent editor. Use **Switch on for an agent** from the card menu as a shortcut.\n\n#### Google Sheets\n\nEvery enquiry lands as a row in a spreadsheet in your own Google Drive.\n\n1. Optionally switch on **Use an existing sheet** and paste its link. Otherwise a new \"(your company) — Enquiries\" sheet is created.\n2. Choose **Connect with Google** and allow access.\n3. Turn on the sheet tool for the agents that should log enquiries.\n\nYou can **Change sheet** or **Start a new sheet** later.\n\n#### Google Calendar\n\nAgents offer real free slots from your calendar and book the meeting, with a Google Meet link. Slots are between 9:00 and 18:00 in your workspace timezone. Optionally **Email a confirmation**. Connect with Google, then turn on the calendar tools for an agent.\n\n#### Google Drive\n\nAgents find a brochure or price list in Drive and send the customer the link. After connecting, put your files in the folder Magic Agent creates. Only that folder and its subfolders are searched.\n\n#### Razorpay\n\nTake payments with payment links.\n\n1. Enter your **Key ID** and **Key Secret** and choose **Connect Razorpay**.\n2. In Razorpay, under **Webhooks**, add the **Webhook URL** and **Webhook secret** shown.\n3. Choose your options:\n- Razorpay texts the link\n- Razorpay emails the link\n- **Links expire after** 1 to 30 days\n- **When an order is paid, move it to** a stage\n\n**Payments** then appears under Leads. See Orders and payments.\n\n#### Magic Forms\n\nAgents send a form in the chat, and the answers come back into the conversation.\n\n1. In Magic Forms, open your workspace's **API → Keys** and create a key.\n2. Paste it as the **API key** and choose **Connect**.\n3. Turn on *send_form* for an agent. Optionally **Reply when it comes back**.\n\nUnder **Submissions**, choose **Save to book** to collect a form's answers in a record book.\n\n#### Magic Reward\n\nAgents send a customer a live offer to play for a prize. Create a key in Magic Reward under **Settings → API keys**, paste it here, then turn on *send_offer* for an agent.\n\n#### Other tools\n\nSlack, Zapier, webhooks, Notion, and Claude and ChatGPT are covered by guidance cards that point you to:\n\n- a custom tool;\n- your webhook settings;\n- the AI assistant connector.\n\n## Team and account\n\n### Team\n\nThe Team page shows everyone who answers for your business: the AI agents that reply on their own, and the human agents who step in. Open it from **Team** in the sidebar.\n\nAI agent cards are labelled **Front desk**, **Follow-up desk**, **Marketing desk** or **AI agent**, with their role, message count and last reply. Choose **Configure** to open the agent editor.\n\n#### Add a human agent\n\nChoose **Add a human agent** and fill in:\n\n| Field | Notes |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Photo** | Upload, or paste an image link |\n| **Name** and **Role** | Shown in the inbox and on replies they sign |\n| **Email** | Their own login uses this |\n| **Phone** and **Note** | Optional |\n| **Status** | **Active**, **Away** (skipped by handover rules) or **Inactive** |\n\nSetting someone to **Inactive** removes them from the list you can reply as, stops their login working, and frees their seat on your plan.\n\n##### Give them a login\n\nFrom the card's menu, choose **Generate login**. The email (or username) and password are shown **once**. Choose **Copy all sign-in details** and pass them on.\n\nTheir replies are signed with their own name. Without a role they can use the whole console, except the workspace password, logins and the plan. From the same menu you can **Reset password** (which also turns off their two-factor) or **Revoke login**.\n\n##### When seats are full\n\nIf your plan's human seats are used up, you'll see **Your human agent seats are full**. Add one extra seat, or upgrade your plan.\n\n#### Roles\n\nA role decides what a human agent sees and can change when they sign in with their own login, on the web and in the app. Choose **Roles** to manage them. Only the workspace admin can.\n\nYour workspace starts with two:\n\n- **Manager**: every chat, and every area.\n- **Agent**: chats assigned to them plus unassigned ones, the Inbox, and Leads to look at.\n\nChoose **Add role**, or the pencil on a role, and set:\n\n| Setting | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Chats they see** | **All chats**, **Assigned to them, and unassigned**, or **Only chats assigned to them**. Applies to the inbox, escalations, leads, alerts and the app. |\n| **Areas** | For each sidebar area: **Hidden** takes it off their sidebar, **View** shows it without changes, **Edit** lets them change it. |\n| **Assign chats to other people** | Without it they can still take a chat or let go of their own. |\n| **Delete and reset chats** | Shows **Delete conversation**. |\n| **Export contacts** | Shows the CSV export on contacts and record books. |\n\nTo give someone a role, open the menu on their card and choose **Role**. **No role** keeps the old behaviour: everything except billing and logins. A role still held by someone can't be deleted. Move them to another role first.\n\n#### Handover rules\n\nChoose **Handover rules** to decide who gets a conversation when an agent escalates it. See Escalations.\n\n#### Remove someone\n\nChoose **Remove** from the card's menu. Replies they already sent stay as the customer saw them.\n\n### Workspace settings\n\nOpen settings from the profile menu at the bottom of the sidebar: **Workspace settings**.\n\n#### Access\n\n- **Workspace access** shows your workspace ID, when the login was issued and last used, and how many sessions are open. A login can be open in one place at a time.\n- **Change your password**: enter the current password, then a new one of at least 12 characters, twice. If you are still on the password you were issued, you'll be prompted to set your own.\n- **Two-factor authentication**: see Sign in.\n\n#### Conversations\n\n**Message limit**: once a conversation holds this many messages in 24 hours, the agents stop replying until the 24 hours are up. Customer messages are still recorded, and your team can keep answering by hand. The default is 50; set 0 for no limit.\n\n#### Webhook\n\n**Outbound webhook**: Magic Agent POSTs captured orders and escalations as JSON to your **Endpoint URL**, signed so your system can check they're genuine. Use **Send test event** to try it and **Rotate signing secret** to change the secret. **Recent deliveries** shows what was sent.\n\n#### Assistant\n\n**Connect an AI assistant** lets Claude, ChatGPT or another assistant read, configure and reply in your workspace for you.\n\n1. Create the connector to get a private URL. It is shown once.\n2. Add it to your assistant:\n- **Claude.ai**: Customize → Connectors → **+** → Add custom connector. Paste the URL and leave OAuth empty.\n- **ChatGPT**: Settings → Connectors → Create. Paste the URL as the Server URL, with no authentication.\n- **Claude Code** and others: follow the instructions on the tab.\n3. **Revoke** stops the URL immediately.\n\nThe assistant can also upload files you attach to the chat or link to: brochures and pictures for the catalogue, and documents for the knowledge base.\n\nWarning: Anyone with the connector URL can read and change your workspace. Keep it private, and revoke it if it leaks.\n\n#### Theme\n\n- **Appearance**: Light, Dark or System. Applies only to you, in this browser.\n- **Palette**: Green, Amber or Emerald. Applies to everyone in the workspace once you **Save**.\n\n#### Danger zone\n\n**Delete this workspace** permanently removes all agents, knowledge, catalogue, orders, conversations, tools and channels. You must type the workspace name to confirm. This can't be undone.\n\n### Billing\n\nOpen billing from the profile menu: **Billing**. It has three tabs: **Plan**, **Wallet** and **Message usage**.\n\n#### Plan\n\n- **Current plan**: the monthly price with GST, your key dates (free trial ends, paid up to, renews on), and Autopay status.\n- **Agents on your plan**: how many custom agents are live, how many human agents have a login, and extra agents in use. If you are over, you'll see **You're over your plan by …**. Pause a custom agent or revoke a human agent's login, or change your plan.\n- **Choose a plan**: compare plans and pay with Razorpay.\n- **Billing details**: legal name, GSTIN, billing email, phone and address for your invoices.\n- **Payment history**.\n\nOnly the workspace's own login can change the plan. **Cancel plan** is always available; your agents keep answering customers either way.\n\nNote: \nIf a payment fails, the console shows when the dashboard locks. Even when it is locked, **your agents keep answering customers**. Choose a plan to open the console again.\n\n#### Wallet\n\nThe wallet pays for WhatsApp **template** messages (marketing, utility and authentication) and for **Genie wishes**. Ordinary replies inside the 24-hour window always go out.\n\nA Genie wish is one request you give Genie. It costs the same as one marketing message to your home country.\n\n- **Top up**: pick an amount (GST is added).\n- **Auto-recharge**: set a low-balance line and a recharge amount, and the wallet tops itself up. It needs a billing email and phone on the Plan tab.\n- **Wallet history**: top-ups, auto-recharges and any welcome bonus.\n\nWarning: \nWhen the wallet can't cover a template, it is held back, and Genie asks you to top up before it takes a new request. Keep the wallet topped up before a campaign or event.\n\n#### Message usage\n\nWhat you spent and on what: total spent, messages billed, average per message and template messages. It also shows a breakdown by conversation type, a spend-per-day chart, and a ledger of every message, filterable by category. Genie requests are listed as **Genie wish**.\n\n### Get help\n\nOpen support from the profile menu: **Support**. Support tickets are also available in the mobile app.\n\n#### Create a ticket\n\nChoose **New ticket**.\n\n**Describe what is happening**\n\nWrite a **Subject** and a **Description**: what you did, what you expected, and what happened instead. Paste screenshots straight into the description, or add up to 10 **Attachments**.\n\n**Decide on access**\n\nSwitch on **Account access granted** to let the person handling the ticket open your workspace, for 1 hour up to 7 days. Access ends on its own. Only the workspace's own login can grant it.\n\n**Set the type and priority**\n\n**Issue type**: Bug, Feature request, Question, Billing, WhatsApp / channel, Agent behaviour, Account access or Other. **Priority**: Low, Normal, High or Urgent. Urgent asks why.\n\n**Create the ticket**\n\nChoose **Create ticket**. The team replies in the ticket and by email.\n\n#### Follow a ticket\n\n- Reply in the ticket. Replying to a resolved ticket reopens it.\n- If support asks to open your workspace, choose **Allow access** (pick how long) or **Decline**. **End access now** stops it early.\n- **Shared credentials**: share another account's login (for example Meta Business) securely. Only the handler can see it, and it is deleted when access ends.\n- **Mark resolved** when you're done, and rate the help from 1 to 5.\n\n#### Access log\n\nThe **Access log** tab lists every time you granted access, every visit by support staff and every time shared credentials were viewed.\n\n# Mobile app\n\n## Magic Agent app\n\n### \n\n---\ntitle: \"The Magic Agent app\"\nsidebarTitle: \"Overview\"\ndescription: \"Answer customers, move leads and keep an eye on your agents from your phone with the Magic Agent app for iPhone and Android.\"\nkeywords: [\"mobile app\", \"ios\", \"android\", \"phone\", \"push notifications\", \"sign in\"]\nicon: \"smartphone\"\n---\n\nThe Magic Agent app puts your inbox, leads and agents in your pocket. It works with the same workspace as the web console, and everything stays in sync live.\n\nUse the app to:\n\n- get a push notification when a conversation is escalated or a new order or record is filed;\n- read and answer chats, send WhatsApp templates and media, and hand chats back to the agent;\n- move leads and records between stages;\n- ask your agents how the day went;\n- ask Genie to make changes for you, from the Genie button above the tab bar.\n\nSet up agents, the catalogue, the knowledge base and marketing in the web console.\n\n#### Sign in\n\n<div>\n1. Install **Magic Agent** from the App Store or Google Play.\n2. The first time you open the app, swipe through the four welcome screens and tap **Get started**, or tap **Skip**.\n3. Enter your **email or workspace ID** and **password**, then tap **Sign in**.\n4. If two-factor is on, enter the six-digit code.\n5. Allow notifications when asked, so you hear about escalations and new orders.\n\nA login can be open on one device at a time. If it's open elsewhere, the app shows **Already signed in elsewhere**. Tap **Sign out the other device** to continue here.\n</div>\n\n#### Getting around\n\nThe tab bar at the bottom has five tabs:\n\n| Tab | What it is for |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Home** | Today's numbers and anything waiting on you. See Home |\n| **Chats** | Every conversation, and replying. See Chats |\n| **Team** | Your AI agents and people, and chatting with an agent about your workspace. See Team |\n| **Leads** | The pipeline, your record books and the catalogue. See Leads |\n| **Profile** | Your account, billing, support, appearance and security. See Profile |\n\n#### Notifications\n\nOn Android, notifications come in three channels you can tune in your phone's settings:\n\n- **Escalations**: a chat handed to a person. A distinct sound and a heads-up banner.\n- **New orders**: an order or record filed.\n- **Everything else**.\n\nTapping a notification opens what it's about: the chat, Leads → Orders, the record book, or a support ticket.\n\n#### Who sees what\n\n| Signed in as | What changes |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Owner** (workspace login) | Everything, including changing the logo, choosing who a reply is signed as, granting support access and managing the plan |\n| **Team member** (own email) | Replies are always signed with your own name. You can't change the logo, grant support access or change the plan |\n\nIf you can reach more than one workspace, tap the company name on Home and choose **Switch workspace**. Every screen follows the workspace you pick.\n\nNote: \nWhen an update is ready, a banner offers **Restart** to get the latest version, or **Later**.\n\n### Home\n\n<div>\nFrom top to bottom, Home shows:\n\n- **A greeting and your company**. Tap the company name to switch workspace, if you can reach more than one.\n- **The bell** (top right) opens Notifications. A pulsing red dot means something new arrived.\n- **A billing banner**, only when it matters: a trial ending, a payment due, or a low wallet. Tap it to open Billing.\n- **Conversations**: how many agents are answering, the total for the period with the change from the period before, and a chart. Drag your finger across the chart to read a single day. Tap **7D**, **14D** or **30D** at the top right of the card to change the period; every figure on Home follows it.\n- **Messages** and **Handed to a human**, each with its trend.\n- **Waiting on you**: escalated chats tagged **Needs you**. Tap one to open it. When nothing is escalated, it says **All clear**.\n</div>\n\n#### Notifications\n\n<div>\nThe bell opens everything sent to your workspace in the last 30 days, newest first, split into **New** and **Earlier**:\n\n- new orders and filed records, such as a site visit or a unit booking;\n- escalations, tinted red;\n- unanswered questions (knowledge gaps);\n- announcements from Magic Agent.\n\nTap an item to open what it's about. Items count as seen when you leave the screen.\n</div>\n\n### \n\n---\ntitle: \"Genie in the app\"\nsidebarTitle: \"Genie\"\ndescription: \"Ask Genie from your phone, by typing or by voice, to set up and run your workspace, and approve each change with a tap.\"\nkeywords: [\"app genie\", \"assistant\", \"ai assistant\", \"approve changes\", \"sparkle button\", \"voice\", \"shake\", \"talk to genie\"]\nicon: \"sparkles\"\n---\n\nGenie is the assistant built into Magic Agent. On the app, tap the **Genie button** with the blinking Magic Agent logo that floats above the tab bar, on the right, from any tab.\n\nAsk in your own words, for example \"Add our refund policy\", \"Move Pooja Joshi to Negotiation\" or \"How did this week go?\". Tap a suggestion such as **Set up my business** to start, or tap the round arrows button next to them for other suggestions. See Genie for everything it can do.\n\n#### Talk to Genie\n\nShake your phone from anywhere in the app to open Genie and start talking. Inside Genie, tap the **microphone** button next to the message box when it is empty.\n\nThe first time, Genie asks to use the microphone: tap **Allow microphone** and accept. If you turned the microphone off for Magic Agent before, tap **Open Settings**, allow it, and come back; voice mode starts on its own.\n\nThe voice screen shows a glowing orb that moves with your voice while Genie listens, swirls while it thinks and pulses while it speaks:\n\n- Just speak. Genie knows you have finished when you pause, then answers out loud in a few short sentences; ask if you want more detail. Its words appear under the orb and light up as Genie says them.\n- Talk over Genie, or tap the orb, to interrupt it. Genie stops and listens.\n- When Genie needs your approval, it reads the change out. Say **yes** or **no**, or tap **Approve** or **Decline**.\n- Tap the **microphone** button at the bottom to mute yourself. Genie stops listening, but still finishes what it is saying. Tap it again, or tap the orb, to talk.\n- Tap the **keyboard** button to switch to typing, or the red **×** to end voice mode.\n\nEverything you say is saved in the chat like a typed message.\n\nNote: \nEvery workspace gets **30 free minutes** of talking to Genie, counted across both your voice and Genie's. The voice screen shows the minutes left. Once they are used up, you can keep typing to Genie. Each request still costs a Genie wish, whether you type it or say it.\n\n#### Approving changes\n\nGenie reads your workspace freely, but asks before it changes anything. Each change appears as a card with what will be saved:\n\n- Tap **Approve** to make the change, or **Decline** to skip it.\n- When several changes are waiting, use **Approve all** or **Decline all** above the message box.\n- Typing a new message instead declines the waiting change.\n\nUnder each reply, Genie lists what it did: **Looked up**, **Done**, **Declined** or **Failed**. Tap a line for the details. Tap **Stop** while Genie is working to stop it.\n\n#### Photos\n\nTap the photo button next to the message box to attach up to five photos. Genie can read a price list or menu and add the products to your catalogue.\n\n#### Your chats\n\nTap the list button at the top to see your chats with Genie, grouped into **Pinned**, **Today**, **Yesterday**, **Previous 7 days** and so on. Your chats are private to your login.\n\n- Tap **New chat** to start another.\n- Use **Search chats** to find an older one by its name.\n- Tap **⋯** on a chat, or press and hold it, to **Pin to top**, **Rename** or **Delete** it.\n- A chat with an amber dot has a change waiting for your approval.\n- Turn on **Apply changes without asking** to let Genie make changes in the open chat straight away. Deleting still asks first.\n\nTap **×** at the top left to close Genie and go back to your tabs.\n\n### Chats\n\n#### The chat list\n\n<div>\n**Chats** lists every conversation your agents are having.\n\n- **Search conversations** by name or message.\n- Filter: **All**, **Escalated**, **WhatsApp**, **Instagram**, **Messenger**, **RCS** or **Telegram**.\n- Tap a **tag chip** (for example *Hot lead*) to show only those leads. Tap it again to clear.\n\nEach row shows the contact, channel and time, a preview, the agent holding it and message count, plus badges: **Needs you** (escalated), **Routed** (the front desk passed it to a specialist), tags and **Resolved**.\n</div>\n\n#### Notifications\n\nTap **Notifications** at the top right, beside the title, to see every alert, test and message sent by hand — who it went to, when, and whether it went. You see this switch only if your role can open Notifications.\n\n- **Search** by number, email, template or words from the message.\n- Tap **Filters** beside the search box to open the filter sheet:\n- **Status**: **All**, **Sent**, **Failed** or **Skipped**, each with its count.\n- **Alert**: one alert, or **Tests** or **Sent by hand**. Tap it again to clear.\n- **Period** (**Today**, **7 days**, **30 days**) and **Channel** (**WhatsApp** or **Email**).\n- **Reset** clears the sheet; **Show results** closes it. The button shows how many filters are on.\n- **Clear filters** under the search resets the filters and the search. Scroll down and older sends keep loading.\n\nTap a send to see the full message — a WhatsApp send shows as the bubble the customer received, on the chat background — and — for anything that didn't go — **Why it did not send**.\n\n#### Read and reply\n\n<div>\nThe customer is on the left and your business on the right. Each run of messages is labelled with who wrote it: an agent, or a team member. Buttons, photos, voice notes, documents and locations show as the customer saw them.\n\n- **Swipe a message right** to quote it in your reply.\n- **Long-press a message** to select it. On an agent's reply, choose **Mark as wrong** or **Fix answer**. On a customer's WhatsApp message, react with an emoji.\n- The **⋮** menu has **View profile**, **Search**, **Chat status**, **Resume** the agent, **Mark as bot** and **Reply settings**.\n</div>\n\n##### Taking over\n\n<div>\n**Sending a reply takes over the chat.** The agent goes quiet for the pause time, then takes the chat back on its own. The strip above the box shows **You have this chat** with the time left. Tap **Resume** to hand it back sooner.\n\nTap the line under the box (for example *Replying as Rohan · pauses Priya for 1 hour*) to open **Reply settings**:\n\n- **Replying as**: whose name signs the reply (workspace password logins only — your own account always replies as you).\n- **Each reply pauses the agent for**: 15 minutes up to 24 hours. Remembered on this phone.\n</div>\n\n##### WhatsApp extras\n\n- The **+** button sends a **Template** (reaches people any time, even after 24 hours), a **Photo**, **Video**, **Location**, **Contact**, **Buttons**, a **Link button** or **Ask location**.\n- The bar above the box shows the **reply window**. When it is closed, free-form text is locked; send a template with **+** instead.\n- **✦** drafts a reply on your phone using an on-device model. You always review it before sending.\n\n##### Escalated chats\n\n<div>\nEscalated chats show a red **escalated** badge and appear under **Waiting on you** on Home and the **Escalated** filter.\n\nReply to the customer, then open **⋮ → Chat status** and choose:\n\n- **Open**: in progress as usual;\n- **Escalated**: waiting on a person;\n- **Resolved**: nothing left to do.\n</div>\n\n#### Contact info\n\n<div>\nTap the contact's name at the top of a chat.\n\n- **Call**, **WhatsApp**, **Email** or **Search** the chat.\n- **Note**: anything the team should know. Shared with everyone, in the app and the console.\n- **Details**: phone, email, company, birthday, customer since.\n- **Collected by the agents**: whatever the agents saved.\n- **Conversation**: status, who's answering, lead stage and why it was filed there.\n</div>\n\n### Leads\n\nThe **Leads** tab has a row of sections across the top: **Stages** (the pipeline), one section per record book with its count (for example **Callbacks**, **Site Visits**, **Unit Bookings** or **Orders**), and **Catalogue**.\n\n#### Stages\n\n<div>\n- **Stage chips** show how many leads sit at each stage. Tap one to filter; tap it again to go back to **All**. **Not yet reviewed** holds chats the follow-up desk hasn't read.\n- **Search leads…** and **Filters**: channel, status and last heard.\n- Each card shows the contact, last message, message count, **Needs you** if escalated, and a **stage pill**.\n\nTap the stage pill to **move** the lead. Filing by hand pins it, so the follow-up desk won't move it. Choose **Unfiled** to let the desk decide again.\n</div>\n\n<div>\nTap a card to open the lead:\n\n- why it was filed at this stage;\n- follow-up status (for example *Stage is closed* or *Can still be nudged*);\n- the last message, who handled it, activity and follow-ups sent.\n\nChoose **Open conversation** or **Move to a stage**.\n</div>\n\n#### Record books\n\nPick a book to see its records. Search by name, phone or reference, and filter by stage. Each card shows the reference, stage, the person and the first details.\n\nTap a record to see every detail and note. Tap a **Stage** chip to move it, for example from *Requested* to *Confirmed*. **Open conversation** jumps to the chat it came from.\n\n#### Catalogue\n\n<div>\nA read-only view of your catalogue, with each entry's category, price and unit. Tap one to see its pictures, description and tags.\n\nEdit the catalogue in the web console.\n</div>\n\n### Team and agent chat\n\n<div>\n**Team** lists everyone who answers for you, under two headings: **AI agents** and **People**.\n\nAgents are listed in order: the front desk, your specialists, the follow-up desk and the marketing desk. Each card shows the agent's status (*Active*, *Paused* or *Draft*), name, role, seat and message count.\n\n- Tap **⋯** for the agent's brief: objective, message and conversation counts, and its last reply.\n- Tap a **person** for their replies sent, time on the team, notes and contact details.\n\nAdd or edit people and agents in the web console.\n</div>\n\n#### Ask an agent about your workspace\n\nTap an agent card to chat with it about your business. The agent reads your workspace data and answers, but it can't change anything from here.\n\nTap a starter such as **How did today go?**, **Anything waiting on me?**, **Summarise today's conversations** or **What came in this week?**, or type your own question. The thread is kept between visits. **Clear** wipes it after a second tap to confirm.\n\n### Profile, billing and support\n\n<div>\nThe green card shows your logo, name and tagline, whether you are the **Owner** or a **Team member**, and conversations, agents live and member since. Owners can tap the logo to change it.\n\n**Account**\n\n- **Your name**: how the agents greet you when they talk to you.\n- **What the agents know**: the company facts every agent reads.\n- **Plan and wallet**: opens Billing.\n- **Help & support**: opens your tickets.\n\n**Business** shows your company details, read-only. Change them in the web console.\n</div>\n\n#### Preferences and security\n\n- **Appearance**: Light, Dark or System.\n- **On-device models** (phones only): see below.\n- **Two-factor authentication**: tap **Set up an authenticator app**, add the key to your authenticator, enter the six-digit code and tap **Turn on**. Save the recovery codes; they're shown only once.\n- **Sign out**: at the bottom. It also stops push notifications on this phone.\n\n#### On-device models\n\nDownload a small AI model that runs entirely on your phone and drafts replies behind the **✦** button in a chat. Nothing in a conversation leaves the phone, and drafting works offline.\n\n| Model | Size | Suits |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Magic Agent Local Lite | about 806 MB | Quick drafts on most phones with 4 GB+ memory |\n| Magic Agent Local Pro | about 1.1 GB | Better drafts, a little slower, phones with 6 GB+ memory |\n\nTap **Download**, then **Use for drafts**. A model loads the first time you ask for a draft and unloads when the app goes to the background.\n\n#### Billing\n\n<div>\nBilling in the app is a read-only view of:\n\n- **Plan**: plan, price, key dates, and how many custom and human agents you use against the plan.\n- **Wallet**: balance, auto-recharge, warnings when the balance is low.\n- **Message usage**: spend over 7, 30 or 90 days, split by template type.\n- **Payment history**.\n\nOwners can tap **Manage plan** or **Top up** to pay in the web console. These buttons don't appear on iPhone.\n</div>\n\n#### Help and support\n\nTap **+ New** to raise a ticket:\n\n1. Write a subject and describe what happened.\n2. Optionally **Add from photos** to attach up to 10 screenshots.\n3. Pick an **Issue type** and **Priority**.\n4. Optionally switch on **Grant account access** for 4 hours to 7 days (owners only).\n5. Tap **Create ticket**. Your device and app version are attached for you.\n\nThe team replies in the ticket and by email. Tap **Resolve** when you're done, and rate the help.";
